From: nvidia-prolapse <nvidia-prolapse@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] gbm_mesa: CPU usage does not force LINEAR on GPU render targets

Applies to https://github.com/waydroid/android_external_minigbm
16844babfbd83d7c206ca22256257cbf26ca7de1 ("gralloc: Handle PixelFormat::R_8").

gbm_mesa_bo_create() set force_linear for every buffer with BO_USE_SW_MASK.
A buffer the GPU renders into (BO_USE_RENDERING / BO_USE_FRONT_RENDERING)
that is also CPU-mapped then becomes LINEAR, which a GPU may not be able to
render to (NVIDIA's EGL imports LINEAR dma-bufs external-only). Keep
needs_map_stride for every CPU-mapped buffer, but force LINEAR only when the
GPU does not render into it; the wrapper's map/unmap provide the linear CPU
view of a tiled buffer and out_map_stride its pitch. Spoofed formats (the R8
carrier) stay LINEAR as before.

---
--- a/gbm_mesa_driver/gbm_mesa_internals.cpp
+++ b/gbm_mesa_driver/gbm_mesa_internals.cpp
@@ -319,13 +319,24 @@
 
 	auto wr = drv->wrapper;
 
+	/*
+	 * CPU access needs a mappable buffer (needs_map_stride), but it forces a
+	 * LINEAR layout only when the GPU does not also render into the buffer.
+	 * A render target with CPU usage (e.g. SurfaceFlinger's screenshot buffer,
+	 * SW_READ/WRITE_OFTEN | HW_RENDER) keeps the layout the backend chooses;
+	 * the backend's map/unmap provide the linear CPU view (as Mesa's
+	 * gbm_bo_map does for tiled buffers) and out_map_stride its pitch.
+	 */
+	const bool sw_access = (use_flags & BO_USE_SW_MASK) != 0;
+	const bool gpu_render = (use_flags & (BO_USE_RENDERING | BO_USE_FRONT_RENDERING)) != 0;
+
 	struct alloc_args alloc_args = {
 		.gbm = drv->gbm_dev,
 		.width = width,
 		.height = height,
 		.drm_format = wr->get_gbm_format(format) ? format : 0,
-		.force_linear = (use_flags & BO_USE_SW_MASK) != 0,
-		.needs_map_stride = (use_flags & BO_USE_SW_MASK) != 0,
+		.force_linear = sw_access && !gpu_render,
+		.needs_map_stride = sw_access,
 		.use_scanout = (use_flags & BO_USE_SCANOUT) != 0,
 	};
 
